# MBProgressHUD

[![SwiftPM compatible](https://img.shields.io/badge/SwiftPM-compatible-brightgreen.svg)](https://github.com/apple/swift-package-manager) [![Carthage compatible](https://img.shields.io/badge/Carthage-compatible-4BC51D.svg?style=flat)](https://github.com/Carthage/Carthage#adding-frameworks-to-an-application) [![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-blue.svg)](http://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)

`MBProgressHUD` is an iOS drop-in class that displays a translucent HUD with an indicator and/or labels while work is being done in a background thread. The HUD is meant as a replacement for the undocumented, private `UIKit` `UIProgressHUD` with some additional features.

This repository is an Objective-C fork of [Matej Bukovinski's MBProgressHUD](https://github.com/matej/MBProgressHUD), targeting **2.0.0 (unreleased)**. It retains the original attribution and MIT license. Configuration and validation are local; the version tag and private Specs release have not been published.

